midori-performance-title = Performance
midori-performance-intro = Choose how Midori shares your computer’s resources.
midori-performance-profile = Performance profile
midori-performance-base = Settings to start from
midori-performance-profile-0 = Performance
midori-performance-profile-1 = Balanced
midori-performance-profile-2 = Memory saving
midori-performance-profile-3 = Gaming / AI
midori-performance-profile-4 = Custom
midori-performance-description-0 = Use your original browser settings. Resource limits stay off unless you enable them.
midori-performance-description-1 = Fewer content processes and smaller caches. Some settings require a restart.
midori-performance-description-2 = Smaller caches and less speculative loading. Pages may load more slowly. Some settings require a restart.
midori-performance-description-3 = More capacity for demanding websites. Some settings require a restart.
midori-performance-memory = Memory
midori-performance-memory-enable = Use a memory budget
midori-performance-budget = Memory budget (GiB)
midori-performance-memory-explanation = A flexible budget unloads eligible inactive tabs. Protected tasks may keep usage above the budget. This is not a hard limit.
midori-performance-cpu = CPU
midori-performance-cpu-explanation = Combined CPU time across Midori’s processes, as a percentage of the logical CPUs reported by the system.
midori-performance-cpu-available-explanation = Combined CPU time across Midori’s processes, as a percentage of the main process’s allowed logical CPUs ({ NUMBER($capacity, maximumFractionDigits: 2) }).
midori-performance-cpu-quota-explanation = Combined CPU time across Midori’s processes, normalized to the main process’s visible CPU allowance ({ NUMBER($capacity, maximumFractionDigits: 3) } CPU equivalents).
midori-performance-native-pending = CPU and network limits require a native backend and are not enabled in this build.
midori-performance-processes = Processes using the most memory
midori-performance-tabs = Tabs using the most resources
midori-performance-tabs-scope = Web tabs in this window. Values describe the associated processes and may be shared with other tabs.
midori-performance-sort = Sort by
midori-performance-tabs-empty = No loaded web tabs in this window.
midori-performance-tab-shared = Shared process usage
midori-performance-tab-suspend = Unload
midori-performance-tab-close = Close
midori-performance-tab-suspended = The tab was unloaded. Select it to load the page again.
midori-performance-tab-protected = This tab cannot be safely unloaded right now.
midori-performance-shared = A process can contain more than one tab. Shared memory is not assigned to individual tabs.
midori-performance-apply = Apply changes
midori-performance-cancel = Discard changes
midori-performance-open-center = Open Midori Center
midori-performance-measurement-commit = Committed memory across Midori’s processes.
midori-performance-measurement-process-memory = Process memory reported by Gecko. This is not a measurement of all physical memory used by the browser.
midori-performance-state-off = Memory budget is off.
midori-performance-state-monitoring = Memory budget is active.
midori-performance-state-reclaiming = Releasing unused resources and eligible inactive tabs to recover memory.
midori-performance-state-blocked = No inactive tab can be safely unloaded at this time.
midori-performance-state-error = Memory could not be checked. Recovery will resume when measurements are available.
midori-performance-measurement-error = Resource usage could not be updated.
midori-performance-conflict = Updated to the latest settings from another view.
midori-performance-applied = Saved automatically.
midori-performance-applied-restart = Changes applied. Restart Midori to apply the profile’s process and cache settings to existing pages.
midori-performance-cancelled = Draft discarded.
midori-performance-apply-error = Changes could not be applied. The previous settings were restored.
midori-performance-sidebar-button =
    .label = Performance
    .tooltiptext = Performance and resource usage
    .aria-label = Performance and resource usage
midori-performance-sidebar-visible =
    .label = Show Performance

midori-performance-sidebar-visible-text = Show Performance in the sidebar
midori-performance-paused-title = Page paused to recover memory
midori-performance-paused-explanation = Midori released this page from memory. Resume it to restore its address, history and saved form fields. Temporary page activity starts again.
midori-performance-paused-resume = Resume page
midori-performance-paused-settings = Change memory budget
midori-performance-paused-error = The page could not be restored. Try again.

midori-performance-memory-strict = Prioritize the memory budget
midori-performance-memory-strict-unavailable = Memory budget priority saved. Prepare Linux memory control to track the browser's full usage. Browsing remains available.
midori-performance-memory-applied = Current effective limit: { $limit } GiB.
midori-performance-measurement-managed-memory = Memory tracked by the limiter, including charged cache and system buffers.
midori-performance-memory-setup-button = Prepare memory control
midori-performance-memory-setup-idle = Prepare memory control for your Linux account. Your system may ask for administrator authentication.
midori-performance-memory-setup-checking = Checking memory control availability…
midori-performance-memory-setup-authenticating = Complete the administrator authentication requested by your system.
midori-performance-memory-setup-session-required = Preparation is saved. Save your work and restart your computer to start a fresh session, then open Midori from the applications menu. Check the limit status above; preparation does not apply a strict limit in this session.
midori-performance-memory-setup-cancelled = Authentication was cancelled. Your resource settings are still saved.
midori-performance-memory-setup-not-installed = Install the Midori DEB or RPM and your system’s pkexec package to prepare memory control from this panel.
midori-performance-memory-setup-error = Memory preparation could not be completed. Your system may have an existing policy, unavailable accounting or no authentication agent. Your resource settings are still saved.
midori-performance-memory-setup-ready = Memory control support is available in this session. Check the limit status above.
midori-performance-cpu-enable = Limit CPU usage
midori-performance-cpu-budget = CPU limit
midori-performance-cpu-unavailable = Saved, pending system support. CPU usage is currently not capped.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-button = Prepare CPU control
midori-performance-cpu-setup-idle = Prepare CPU control for your Linux account. Your system may ask for administrator authentication.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-checking = Checking CPU control availability…
midori-performance-cpu-setup-authenticating = Complete the administrator authentication requested by your system.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-session-required = Preparation is saved. Save your work and restart your computer to start a fresh session, then open Midori from the applications menu. CPU usage is not capped in this session.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-cancelled = Authentication was cancelled. Your resource settings are still saved; CPU usage is not capped.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-not-installed = Install the Midori DEB or RPM and your system’s pkexec package to prepare CPU control from this panel.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-error = CPU preparation could not be completed. Your system may have an existing policy or no authentication agent. Your resource settings are still saved.
midori-performance-cpu-setup-ready = CPU control is available in this session. Check the limit status above.
